    'brain.note.knn': 'Keeps the training examples. For a new input, its k nearest examples vote for a class. Inspect which neighbours voted and their distances. It can classify unseen inputs, but cannot invent a class it was never taught.',
    'brain.note.proto': 'Keeps the average feature vector of each class and chooses the closest average. Inspect the distances to these class centres. One average can hide differences within a class.',
    'brain.note.neural': 'Learns weights that connect input features, hidden units and class outputs. Inspect their responses for one input. Output scores show how the model divides its prediction between classes; they are not a guarantee of correctness.',
    'brain.note.number': 'Reads the training answers as numbers and predicts their average among the nearest examples. It can return a number that no training example had, but stays within the neighbours’ answer range.',
    'brain.note.line': 'Fits a rule to predict a numerical answer. Degree 1 gives a straight line; higher degrees can bend it. The penalty discourages large weights. It can predict beyond the training range, where predictions may be unreliable.',
    'brain.note.grouper': 'Ignores the training labels and groups examples into k clusters by their features. Inspect the cluster centres and which is closest. A cluster is a similarity group, not a class someone taught it.',
