    // what listening does.
    'consent.stt.title': 'Let the Microphone listen?',
    // Final review, finding 2 (IMPORTANT): the shipped body had softened "over the internet" down
    // to "to its own speech service" — the ONE fact spec §6 and plan R6 both word explicitly
    // ("the browser's speech service over the internet" / "the browser's ONLINE speech service"),
    // and the one thing this whole consent moment exists to disclose (cloud STT off unless
    // consented). Restored, plainly, in both string files.
    'consent.stt.body': 'When a Microphone listens, this browser sends what you say over the internet to its own speech service so it can turn it into a word. Nothing is recorded or kept — only that one word comes back.',
    'consent.stt.allow': 'Allow',
    'consent.stt.notNow': 'Not now',
    // THE MICROPHONE's own plate control (R6, task 3): the change-your-mind affordance, plain
    // words both directions — reads/writes WorkshopConsent LIVE, never a per-block cache.
    'microphone.consentOn': 'Speech listening is on for this device.',
    'microphone.consentOff': 'Speech listening is off for this device.',
    'microphone.turnOn': 'Turn it on',
    'microphone.turnOff': 'Turn it off',
    // THE MICROPHONE's honest-state cascade (task 3, floor-art.js microphoneBox — dead-surface
    // law): floor-art.js never calls t(), so these travel through floorBridge()'s `words` map,
    // exactly like board.noWire/board.noWatch/… above. Priority order (highest first): listening
    // (live) → blocked (re-derived from WorkshopConsent, never the stale per-block hint) → the
    // heard word itself → heard-nothing, SPLIT in two by device capability (breaker fix round,
    // charter 5 RULED IN: `probe().listen` already knows a device with zero speech recognition
    // from one that simply missed an utterance — the toolbox knew, game.js just never asked) →
    // never listened at all.
    'microphone.listening': 'Listening…',
    'microphone.blocked': 'Speech is off — change it on my plate.',
    'microphone.heardNothing': 'Didn’t catch that.',
    // Distinct from heardNothing on purpose (breaker charter 5): a device that can NEVER hear —
    // no Web Speech recognizer at all — must never say "try again" forever with no honest reason.
    'microphone.noDevice': 'This browser has no speech service — the Microphone cannot hear here.',
    'microphone.neverListened': 'Poke me, or wire a Button to listen.',
    // THE SPEAKER's own honest-device sentence (task 064 T2, floor-art.js speakerBox): the
    // Microphone's noDevice caption above has a sibling here — a device with no TTS at all must
    // say so in words, the same small-caption idiom, rather than just going silently mute.
    'speaker.noVoice': 'No voice here — the word shows instead.',
    // THE FRAME's two honest face sentences (Composing Arc Plan C, task 3, floor-art.js frameBox
    // — the dead-surface law: an empty panel reads as broken, so there is no blank state). Like
    // the Board's and the Microphone's captions, floor-art.js never calls t(), so both travel
    // through floorBridge()'s `words` map.
    //   empty     — nothing has been handed to this Frame in THIS run (its memory is run state,
    //               engine.js createRun — a new Run genuinely starts it empty, and saying so is
    //               the truth, not an apology).
    //   noPicture — it HOLDS an example and there is no image to draw: either the example was
    //               never a photo (a row of numbers, a word) or the photos died with the tab.
    //               Cam.thumbs is memory-only BY LAW (the privacy rule for children's faces), so
    //               this state is permanent after a reload, not a glitch — the words say what the
    //               Frame is showing INSTEAD, and why, without asking to be forgiven for it.
    // BOTH LENGTHS ARE MEASURED ON THE REAL CANVAS, not judged by eye or by character count (fix
    // round 1). A placed Frame is 118.8x97.2 px (fit 0.90) and 92.4x75.6 at FIT_MIN in a crowded
    // room; these are the longest wordings that still paint WHOLE at BOTH — probed at fits 0.70 /
    // 0.80 / 0.90 / 1.0 through floor-art's own draw path. Character count alone does not decide
    // it, which is exactly why guessing failed: "No picture kept, just the name." (31) fits at
    // FIT_MIN while "No picture is kept — the name." (30) does not, because the wrap breaks on
    // WORDS. Re-word either of these and re-probe, or a busy room silently loses the end of it.
    'frame.empty': 'Nothing yet. Wire a nearest example to me.',
