  /**
   * The authored table, compiled into the flat table a Run steps.
   *
   * The compile itself lives in logic/run-session.js (task P5a) — recursive Brick expansion, the
   * checker's Tally shape, the three dealing arms and the latch gate's synthetic levers are the
   * SAME decisions the headless batch runner needs, so they have one owner, reachable from
   * `node --test`, instead of a browser-only copy here and another one there. This wrapper is
   * only what the shell adds: the LIVE table and seed, and `validateLibraryTree` — the library
   * binding check, which cannot move above the headless return because it reads the registries
   * the DOM shell builds. A corrupt brick def or a bad binding throws HERE and is caught at the
   * Run-press site, same as any other bad-table failure (never a silent dead Run button).
   */
